column5:
Fixed erroneous -D use in ParflowTest.cmake

error: "-D={MPIEXEC_PREFLAGS=${MPIEXEC_PREFLAGS}"
fix: -DMPIEXEC_PREFLAGS=${MPIEXEC_PREFLAGS}

Removed duplications on formal parameters, inputs and outputs.

Hopefully all the cases where they were happening have been fixed.

@simleo realized about this problem.

provide a single component → Coordinate ctor (also removes the need for component wise operations)
using op- or op+ with scalars resulted in only the x position getting affected (because the other components were initialized to 0)
this e.g. affected the loading position of skeletons

save magIndex for cube2Pointer access

move hash table type and query function to state
remove hashtable.{cpp,h}

no need for an if

the failing input operations will simply evaluate to false
if the line stream can’t support them (if the color is missing)

some 3d tex render cleanup

resets textures properly without indiscriminatly using
glActiveTexture(GL_TEXTURE0);

- Introduced NeoInEdgeTaredNode
- Added Method to NeoComplexEdge
- Renaming from Neo4JPathPart to NeoPathPart as well as in Neo4JAttributePathPathPart to NeoAttributePathPathPart
- Starting to implement EdgeTest || Tested:
	- generateSimpleEdgeBlank();
	- generateSimpleEdgeWithLabels();
	- generateSimpleEdgeWithDirections();
	- generateSimpleAttributeEdge();
	- generateAttributeEdgeWithSimpleNeoPath();
	- generateAttributeEdgeWithComplexEdgeNeoPath();
	- generateAttributeEdgeWithComplexEdgeNeoPathComplexNodesLabels();

Adding alternate water models to Amber parameters.  The approved model
for Amber is still TIP3P, but if you want reasonable water dynamics,
you need SPC/E.  OOPSE/OpenMD will now give you the choice.
